+# Virtual Mac — RootHide port
+
+This tree adds an experimental RootHide packaging/build path for VirtualMacOniPad.
+
+## Target layout
+
+The package installs the large Virtual Mac runtime at:
+
+    <jbroot>/User/Library/VirtualMac/
+
+The iOS application remains at `<jbroot>/Applications/VirtualMac.app` because SpringBoard/uicache expect a conventional application bundle. VM bundles created by the app remain in `/var/mobile/Media/VirtualMac` so they stay user-owned and survive package removal.
+
+## Build
+
+On a macOS machine with the repository's existing prerequisites:
+
+    export VZ_ROOTHIDE=1
+    ./VirtualMac/scripts/build-ipad-deb-roothide.sh
+
+The script uses the existing build pipeline, compiles the path-aware pieces with `-DVM_ROOTHIDE`, and emits an `iphoneos-arm64e` Debian package.
+
+To build only the app IPA after building the app bundle:
+
+    mkdir -p build/VirtualMac-RootHide/Payload
+    cp -R build/ipad-app/VirtualMac.app build/VirtualMac-RootHide/Payload/
+    cd build/VirtualMac-RootHide
+    zip -qry ../VirtualMac-RootHide.ipa Payload
+
+The IPA is only the GUI/application bundle; it is **not** a replacement for the RootHide Debian package because the VM requires the privileged launcher and runtime payload.
+
+## Important limitation
+
+This environment does not contain Apple's Xcode/iPhoneOS SDK, `xcrun`, `ldid`, or the extracted macOS virtualization inputs required by the upstream project, so the final Mach-O binaries cannot be compiled or tested here. The source and package changes are therefore an experimental port, not a claimed working binary release.
+
+The upstream project currently states that Dopamine-roothide is unsupported, and the upstream issue requesting RootHide support remains open. See the project issue and RootHide developer documentation for the runtime/path model.
